        <p>1</p>
        <p>The following letter will show how un- wise it is for women to submit to the dangers of a surgical operation when often it may be avoided by taking Lydia E. Pink ham's Vegetable Compound. The writer of it was four weeks in the hospital and came home suffer ing worse than before. Here is her own statement "Two years ago I suffered very severely Ilacement. I could not be on my feet fora longtime. My physician treated me for several months without much relief and at last sent me to a hospital for an oper- ation. I was there • four weeks and came home suffering worse than before. My mother advised me to try Lydia E Pink- - ham's Vegetable Corn- an. To-day I am well and strong and do all my own housework. I owe my health to Lydia E. Pin kham's Vegetable Compound and advise my friends who are afflicted with any feinalo ailment to try it." (Name and address on request.)</p>
        <p>_ If you are ill do dot drag along until an operation is necessary, but at once take Lydia E. Pinkham's Vegetable Com- pound. For thirty years it has been the standard remedy for women's ills, and has restored the health of thousand:3, of .suf- fering women. Why don't you try it.? Write to-day for a fre.e.pr:vate book ((o women only) to the Lady Manager, the Lydia E. Pinkham Medicine Co., 42a Hampsteadfiraad, London, N.W. For 2s. 9d. she will send you a bottle of the Lydia E. Pinkham Vegetable Compound, or for 4s. 6d. a much larger bottle. Any chemist will supply it at these prices.</p>
