        <p>lodged from kidneys and removed by Doan's Pills.</p>
        <p>Mr. E. E. MINNS, 7, Shipstone Street, New Basford, Nottingham, says : " After five years' acute suffering from stone in the kidney, I was advised to undergo an operation. But, for a long time, I had been persuaded to try Doan's Backache Kidney Pills, and after lying on my bed , in agony for six weeks I gave the Pills atrial. "To my delight I ' was easier after the second box—then one day I felt the stone dislodged. Later on the stone came from the ' bladder, and with slight assistance was • completely removed. I never remember , feeling so well as now, and shall never be able to praise Doan's Pills enough." (Signed) " E. E. MINNS."</p>
        <p>Three Stones (exact size) removed by Doan's Pills, and serious operation avoided.</p>
