      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1914-01-31_WidnesExaminer_art0036" n="art0036">
        <head>'\Fti</head>
        <p>'\Fti</p>
        <p>Mr. T. J. LEECH, 13, Lypiatt Street, Cheltenham, says have bad three operations for stone, 1890, 1894 and 1900;' but when, recently, I felt signs of the trouble having come again, I decided to try Doan's Backache Kidney Pills. "These Pills did me good at once— and, after a time, they brought away the three stones I am sending to you. But for Doan's Pills I must have had another operation, and I am very grateful for all the Pills have done." (Signed) "T. J. LEECH."</p>
