        <p>t'la re ground at all permits of the Warr_ineg-- A•ol,ll`srwards indulging in their famous tf t 411141• 'Fil'lllas and his merry five ought moo do Z:an, t° l'Pset the Wigan calculations. o h to -R and Owe, Nicholas ought to be equal at least I ezh,s,and Walford. t4—'B gta,t things of the Warrington tlriene- r:l),lll, all.O iY have now got into working . g n'aed si„ tiley are up to the :laartet, ~,"id be quite equal to t expectatp3ns the . 'lasi "i'lo ll'or been strengthened by , , en of ~ _ ehe Colileieirns: who 4'as iniu Jenkins and Bradley. Skelhorne,wi is will k..hisenteet.e(l, at Wilderspool on Saturday, 'nse hi-s' .pit Ctesters has recovered and vi, The Place. 41ti,,,, _lllateli .4 augh . tto prOve a close and ter- -4:4' and there should not be many points illoodn the sides at the close. Warrington IT .41 tea 81".ing chance of securing victory. Ins will be:— •</p>
