        <p>LES BY AUCTION</p>
        <p>AUCTIONEER AND VALUER, BEWSEY CHAMBERS, WARRINGTON. Sales by Auction of Freehold and Leasehold Properties, Building Land, Ground Rents, Farming and Trade Stocks, Household Furni- ture. Stocks, Shares and Debentures. Valuations for Sale, Probate and Mortgage, on reasonable terms.</p>
      </div>
      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1914-01-31_WidnesExaminer_art0189" n="art0189">
        <head>-ROBERT LOWE,</head>
        <p>-ROBERT LOWE,</p>
        <p>ESTATE AGENT. AUCTIONEER &amp; VALUER. MARKET GATE SALEROOMS, 5, BUTTER- M ARKET-STREET, WARRINGTON. Weekly Sales every Wednesday afternoon. Telephone No. 55. Consignments invited.</p>
        <p>I</p>
        <p>By Mr. ROBERT LOWE. TO CATTLE DEALERS AND OTHERS. MARKET GATE SALE ROOMS, 5, BUTTER- MARKET-STREET, WARRINGTON. At 2 o'clock. WEDNESDAY NEXT, FEBRUARY 4. MR. R. LOWE is instructed to SELL BY AUCTION the STOCK-IN-TRADE of HORSE and CATTLE MEDICINES, CONDIMENTS, DISINFECTANTS, FERTI- LIZERS, BRUSHES, STATIONERY,ACCOUNT BOOKS, &amp;c., as follows :-10cwt. Lowe's Fatten- ing Meal, lcwt. Lowe's Calf Meal, 20cwt. Stan- dard Guano Co.'s Fertilizer, 20cwt. Guano Cattle Drinks and Medicines, Condiments, Disinfect- ants, Oils, Medicine Chest, Pig Powders, Worm Powders, Drenches, Electric Lamps, &amp;c. Also a Consignment of HOUSEHOLD FURNITURE, STATIONERY, STEEL SAFE, TWEED CLOTH in Suit lengths, &amp;c. Catalogues on application.</p>
      </div>
      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1914-01-31_WidnesExaminer_art0190" n="art0190">
        <head>By Mr. FRANK HICKMAN.</head>
        <p>By Mr. FRANK HICKMAN.</p>
        <p>THURSDAY NEXT, FEBRUARY sth, 1914. MARKET PLACE, WARRINGTON. SALE BY AUCTION of Surplus Furnishing EFFECTS, removed from No. 50, Arpley- street, by instruction of Mr. Fenton, who is leaving town. The Lots include: Joiners' Tool Chest, Juvenile Trailer, with Pneumatic Tyres and Attachment; Flag Wool. Photographer's Print Washers, Kodak Camera, Gold Swan"" Foun- tain Pen, Chair Bed, 3 Pictures, Coke Anthracite Stove, Overmantel, Bedstead, Adjustable Piano Player, Lot Books, Bound "Graphics," contain- ing South African War; Gent's 'Bicycle, Draw- ing-room Suite in Mahogany and Silk Tapestry, Mahogany Cabinet with Bevel Mirror, Mahogany Ovcrmantel, Scott's Gas Pressure Regulator, Occasional Table, Dresser, Coal Box, "Rich- mond" Gas Stove, Patent Washer and Wringer, Garden Hose, and Sundry Effects. Sale to commence at 2 o'clock prompt. Auctioneer : FRANK HICKMAN. Office: Lyme-street.</p>
        <p>THE HOUSE TO LET.—Particulars apply to AUCTIONEER.</p>
        <p>By Mr. W. BOOTH.</p>
        <p>LEAVING THE PREMISES. 64, and 66, SANKEY-STREET, WARRINGTON THIS DAY and following days until the Stock is cleared. _ .</p>
        <p>MR. W. BOOTH has received instructions from S. Williams and Son, who are giv- ing up business in Warrington, to SELL BY AUCTION the whole of the large and high- class stock of CHINA, GLASS and ART POTTERY WARE. Sale by Auction at 3 and 7 o'clock each day. SHOP TO LET. Fixtures will be Sold on the last day of Sale.</p>
