        <p>MONDAY NEXT, FEBRUARY 2nd, At Eleven p'clock a.m. Re GREER. IN BANKRUPTCY. SALE OF SILCOCK-STREET LOCK WORKS, GOLBORNE. -11 OMAX, SONS &amp; MILLS will SELL BY AUCTION upon the Premises, Silcock- street, Golborne, near Newton-le-Willows, on MONDAY, the 2nd FEBRUARY. 1914, at Eleven o'clock in the forenoon, subject to Conditions to be then and there produced; Lot I.—The Brick-built Premises, known as Sileock-street LOCK WORKS, together with the Outbuildings and Yard, in' the occupation of Messrs. Andrew Greer and Company. The property is leasehold for the residue of a term of 999 years, and the total ground rent payable is .211 7s. Id. The Lot also includes the following FIXED PLANT. 6 h.-p. Gas Engine by Crossley Bros., Ltd.; Coke-crushing Machine, Circular Saw Bench, Drilling Machines, Screw Presses, Turning Lathes, Fitters' Benches, Vices, "Carter's" 18-in. Fan and Piping, Shafting, Pulleys and Fixings, Smiths' Hearths and Appurtenances. Lot 2.—THE LOOSE MACHINERY, TOOLS,, STOCK-IN-TRADE and EFFECTS, comprising : Smiths' Anvils, Swage Blocks, Blacksmiths' Tools, Sledge and Hand Hammers, Platform Weighing Machines, Single Purchase Crab, 2,000 ft. of Flat Bar Iron for Hinges (in lengths), Quantity of Finished and Part Finished Plate Locks, Padlocks, and New Stores. Lot 2 will first be offered in One Lot, and if not so disposed of will be sold piecemeal. For further particulars, and to inspect Schedules, apply to the Auctioneers, Central Chambers, Bolton. and 54, John Dalton-street, Manchester T. 11. Winder. Esq. (Official Re- ceiver), Exchange-street, Bolton; or to Messrs. WOODCOCK, STOBART &amp; Co.. Solicitors, 1, 'Libra-street, Wigan.</p>
