        <head>BAY HORSE.</head>
        <p>THE BAY HORSE.</p>
        <p>The general meeting took place on SaturdaY last. There was a fair crowd present when the President, Mr. 11. Hayes, opened the meeting' The business of the evening included: The bal; aace sheet, paying of prize moneys, election al officers for 1914, and the specials for 1914. For a aociety in its first year, the members may con- gratulate themselves, for they finished up with a substantial balance, and have already together a fair number of specials for thi° season. Their club night for subscriptions is to be held the first Monday in each month.</p>
