        <p>which the toast had been drunk, and he assured them that the governors very much appreciated the kind feeling that had been expressed towards them. Reference had been made- to the need of a site for a new school. Well, he hoped such a site would be found before the century ran out. (Laughter.) At any rate, they might rely upon the gover- nors doing their best to place the school in -more beautiful surroundings. They were fully, alive to the fact that the present situation was not the place for a school of the standing of the Boteter-Granuntii (I,l=sy.vi-e--A rt- c.t....l.44vo,Acurcuild be made th secure a site that would meet- all re- quirements. (Applause.) The town was very rightly proud of the school, which had produced many • of their local leading men, and it was a source of satisfaction to the governors to know that when Grammar School boys had gone out into the world they had acquitted themselves in a manner which had been a credit to the school. (Hear, hear, and applause.)</p>
        <p>LIBERAL PUBLICATIONS. t We have pleasure in directing attention to e various ways in which the Liberal Publica- tl.°ll Department is of service to the Liberal try. The "Liberal Magazine" is issued on 7th of every month and deals in full with the politics of the preceding month. A number costs 6d. post free, the yearly t"°seription is ss. post free. A new volume (the jenty-second) began with the February num- -1,..er• Another special feature which deserves to better known is the Annual Guinea Sub- ni-Ption," in return for which subscribers get ;a) monthly issues of the "Liberal Magazine"; b) at the end of the year a specially bound copy of the "Magazine" on superior paper; (c) copies of all pamphlets and leaflets as issued; (d) para- Phlets and leaflets bound in a volume, printed on buPerior paper and indexed; (e) the monthly issues of the "Liberal Monthly," and (f) the "Liberal Year Book" on superior paper and sPecially bound. For further information as to the Liberal Magazine," the "Guinea Sub- and various other services, applica- tion should be made to the Liberal Publication t/ePartment, 42, Parliament-street, Westmin- ster, S.W.</p>
