        <p>Notices of births, marriages, and deaths, in memoriam notices, and acknowledgments of sympathy are inserted in the " Examiner " at the following rates :—Not exceeding 20 words, Is. 6d. each; every additional seven words, 6d. Deaths. ROBERTS.—On January 23rd, at St. Elphin's, Queensland-road, Boscombe, Bournemouth, after ' a long and painful illness. Mary, the beloved wife of Captain C. J. Roberts, late the King's Regi- ment. ROBINSON.—January 30th. at 'TB. Legh-street, Ellen, widow of the late Joseph Robinson, con- tractor, Warrington. No flowers by request. LYONS.—January 24th, John Lyons, 26, Folly-lane, aged 71 years. SHAW.—January 26th, Florence Shaw, 127, Knuts- ford-road, aged 19 years. JONES.—January 27th, John Alfred Jones, 60, Dud- ley-street, aged 49 years.</p>
        <p>Acknowledgments. CAPTAIN C. J. ROBERTS and FAMILY return hearty THANKS to their friends for the many kind expressions of sympathy extended to them.</p>
