        <p>LYONS INTERNATIONAL URBAN ExH I BITIoN 1914 (May Ist to November Ist). On May Ist, 1914, will be opened in the historic City of Lyons, one of the finest Exhibitions ever held on the Continent. - This Exhibition will be International and urban. It will be the apotheosis of INDUSTRY, SCIENCE and INVENTION. The Exhibition will comprise 30 Magnificent Palaces and Buildings, situated in the splendid Park, at the junction of the Saone and the Rhone. All the nations of the earth are competing for the best positions at this forthcoming 'festival of the Inventor and the Scientist, and thanks to the warm friendship uniting the hands and hearts of the French and British people, THE BRITISH SECTION HAS BEEN ASSIGNED THE PLACE OF HONOUR AT THE MAIN ENTRANCE OF THE EXHIBITION. The magnificent gardens will be one gigantic bouquet of flowers, trees and ornamental shrubs. Some 12,000 gardeners are engaged in the industry of preparing masterpieces for this Exhibition. POSITION. The Exhibition is situated inside the town of Lyons. There will be a fine STADIUM and SPORTS GROUND, also a FUN CITY. As we know all nations vie in the endeavour to capture the trade and get the largest possible share from the coffers of wealthy France. WAKE UPI ENGLAND! Germany, the United States of America, Italy and Russia, not to count the host of less important nations are all taking important Sections. Now is the time to strike, thanks to the present peculiarly favourable situation, to THE ENTENTE CORDIALE to the love and respect to which every Frenchman and French- woman has for Great Britain and her people and products. All applications for space or information should be addressed to The French Chamber of Commerce in London, Monument Square, London, E.O; or British Representative, Lyons International Exhibition, London Chamber of Commerce, Oxford Court, Cannon Street, EC., who can be seen at this address every day from 9 to ix a.m.</p>
